Subject: [PATCH] jz4740_mmc: reduce poll IRQ timeout budget

Testing shows that `jz4740_mmc_poll_irq` code path is exclusively used for CMD53 when used with SDIO Wi-Fi cards.
Under heavy traffic, as much as 70% of operations burn all of the timeout budget, the remaining ones burn majority of that budget.
(after which the code falls back to registering for interrupt)
This leads to heavy CPU overhead.

Reduce the poll budget to 64 iterations. This still leaves a small fast path
for completions that are already visible, while making the driver hand control
back to the interrupt fallback quickly when the controller needs more time.

Before:
-- CPU --
   39     2 root     SW       0   0%  43% [irq/36-13460000]
   69     2 root     SW       0   0%  28% [aicwf_busrx_thr]
   71     2 root     DW       0   0%  10% [ksdioirqd/mmc1]
-- INTERRUPTS --
36 7584/s INTC 36 13460000.mmc
9 1606/s INTC 3 13420000.dma-controller
--- THROUGHPUT: ~9MB/s --

After:
-- CPU --
   71     2 root     SW       0   0%  26% [aicwf_busrx_thr]
   39     2 root     SW       0   0%  13% [irq/36-13460000]
   72     2 root     DW       0   0%  10% [ksdioirqd/mmc1]
-- INTERRUPTS --
36 6467/s INTC 36 13460000.mmc
9 1293/s INTC 3 13420000.dma-controller
--- THROUGHPUT: ~9MB/s --

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
index 58a76ec..cd15f0b 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
@@ -118,6 +118,12 @@
 #define JZ_MMC_DEFAULT_RESTO 0xff
 #define JZ_MMC_DEFAULT_RDTO 0x00ffffff
 #define JZ_MMC_CLKRT0_MIN_RATE 3000000
+/*
+ * Keep the busy-poll window short under sustained SDIO traffic. If the
+ * controller does not report completion quickly, let the interrupt fallback
+ * handle it instead of burning CPU in the threaded IRQ worker.
+ */
+#define JZ_MMC_POLL_IRQ_TIMEOUT 0x40
 
 enum jz4740_mmc_version {
 	JZ_MMC_JZ4730,
@@ -497,7 +503,7 @@ static void jz4740_mmc_request_done(struct jz4740_mmc_host *host)
 static unsigned int jz4740_mmc_poll_irq(struct jz4740_mmc_host *host,
 	unsigned int irq)
 {
-	unsigned int timeout = 0x800;
+	unsigned int timeout = JZ_MMC_POLL_IRQ_TIMEOUT;
 	uint32_t status;
 
 #if 0
